s5-5-p28 = realized (prose (cons "The handler state is \(\mu\). It responds to `Read(a)` with \(\mu[a]\), and to `Write(a,b)` by updating its state to \(\mu[a\mapsto b]\) and returning `Unit`. The source continuation carries no memory. Thus each write occurs exactly once, and the resulting trace is determined by the handler equations." nil)) (cons (cite bm-handle "bm-handle") nil)
